{
  "abstract": "We compute the primitive representation density of a Hermitian Gram at every congruence depth over an unramified quadratic local algebra, including singular reduction and the divided frame at split comparison primes. We derive the normalized genus count and evaluate the signed scalar paired-orbit contribution as a sum of positive packet matrices with explicit density multipliers and one framed automorphism denominator. Under stated trace, real energy, diagonal and arithmetic matrix comparisons on the same unitary period family, these formulas give a bound for the rank of every subset of integral period columns, with explicit source and row losses. This gives a fixed-family spectral input for the period-height argument of rStation paper 194. The separate real and global comparison hypotheses are specified as equations and estimates.",
